   "title": "Gradient as a rate of change",
   "stem": "An oven heats at a constant rate. Its temperature is $20\\,{}^{\\circ}\\mathrm{C}$ when it is switched on and $110\\,{}^{\\circ}\\mathrm{C}$ six minutes later. Let $T$ be the temperature after $t$ minutes.",
   "prompt": "(a) Find the gradient of the line, and interpret it.<br>(b) Write down $T$ in terms of $t$.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "m &= \\frac{110 - 20}{6 - 0}"
      },
      {
       "tex": "&= 15"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "(a) <span class=\"ans\">The temperature rises by $15\\,{}^{\\circ}\\mathrm{C}$ per minute.</span>"
    },
    {
     "text": "(b) <span class=\"ans\">$T = 15t + 20$</span>, since the intercept is the starting temperature."
    }
